window.NEO_FIELDKIT={"unit":"formulae-rearranging","expedition":"The Inventor’s Workshop","tools":[{"title":"Order card","icon":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\"><rect x=\"14\" y=\"12\" width=\"72\" height=\"76\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3e6c4\" stroke=\"#6b4a2c\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><g font-family=\"Georgia\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#3a2a10\" font-size=\"13\"><text x=\"24\" y=\"32\">( )</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"50\">x²</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"68\">× ÷</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"84\">+ −</text></g><path d=\"M66 26 V80 M60 72 L66 82 L72 72\" stroke=\"#2AB3A0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"/></svg>","body":"<p>Work in this order: <b>brackets</b>, then <b>powers</b>, then <b>× and ÷</b>, then <b>+ and −</b>.</p><p>2 + 3 × 4 = 2 + 12 = 14. &nbsp; (2 + 3) × 4 = 5 × 4 = 20.</p><p>When the same kind of operation appears twice, work from left to right.</p>","room":"The Drawing Office","lesson":"Lesson 1 · Letters as unknowns and variables"},{"title":"Cold-store thermometer","icon":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\"><rect x=\"42\" y=\"8\" width=\"16\" height=\"66\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#365a68\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><rect x=\"46\" y=\"40\" width=\"8\" height=\"34\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/><circle cx=\"50\" cy=\"80\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/><g stroke=\"#365a68\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path d=\"M60 20H68M60 32H68M60 44H68M60 56H68\"/></g></svg>","body":"<p>Multiplying or dividing <b>two</b> numbers: if <b>both are negative</b>, the answer is <b>positive</b>; if <b>only one is negative</b>, the answer is <b>negative</b>.</p><p>(−3) × (−4) = 12 &nbsp; · &nbsp; (−3) × 4 = −12 &nbsp; · &nbsp; (−12) ÷ (−3) = 4</p><p>With <b>more than two</b> numbers, work in pairs, or count the negatives: an <b>even</b> number of negatives gives a positive answer, an <b>odd</b> number gives a negative one. (−2) × (−3) × (−4) = 6 × (−4) = −24.</p><p>Put a negative number in <b>brackets</b> when you substitute it: if <i>x</i> = −3, then <i>x</i>² = (−3)² = 9.</p>","room":"The Cold Store","lesson":"Lesson 2 · Substituting positive, negative and fractional values"},{"title":"Notation tag","icon":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\"><path d=\"M14 30 L60 14 L88 52 L44 84 Z\" fill=\"#e9d7a8\" stroke=\"#6b4a2c\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><circle cx=\"58\" cy=\"28\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#6b4a2c\"/><text x=\"46\" y=\"62\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"Georgia\" font-style=\"italic\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#3a2a10\">5b</text></svg>","body":"<p><b>5<i>b</i></b> means 5 × <i>b</i>. &nbsp; <b><i>ab</i></b> means <i>a</i> × <i>b</i>. &nbsp; <b><i>b</i>²</b> means <i>b</i> × <i>b</i>. &nbsp; <b><i>b</i>/2</b> means <i>b</i> ÷ 2.</p><p>The number is written first: 5<i>b</i>, not <i>b</i>5.</p><p>5<i>b</i> + 30 cannot be simplified: 5<i>b</i> and 30 are unlike terms.</p>","room":"The Order Book","lesson":"Lesson 3 · Formulae from words and diagrams"},{"title":"Pattern card","icon":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\"><rect x=\"8\" y=\"22\" width=\"84\" height=\"56\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3e6c4\" stroke=\"#6b4a2c\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><g fill=\"#b0412f\"><rect x=\"16\" y=\"40\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\"/><rect x=\"38\" y=\"40\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\"/><rect x=\"52\" y=\"40\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\"/></g><text x=\"80\" y=\"54\" font-family=\"Georgia\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#3a2a10\">…</text></svg>","body":"<p>For a sequence that goes up by the same amount each time, the <b><i>n</i>th term</b> starts with <b>(the difference) × <i>n</i></b>.</p><p>4, 7, 10, 13, … goes up by 3, so compare with 3<i>n</i>: 3, 6, 9, 12, … Each term is 1 more, so the <i>n</i>th term is 3<i>n</i> + 1.</p><p>Check: when <i>n</i> = 2, 3 × 2 + 1 = 7. ✓</p>","room":"The Pattern Loom","lesson":"Lesson 4 · Deriving a formula"},{"title":"Reversing spanner","icon":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\"><path d=\"M24 76 L62 38\" stroke=\"#8f9aa3\" stroke-width=\"12\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M58 22 a18 18 0 1 0 22 22 l-10 -2 l-6 -6 l-2 -10 z\" fill=\"#8f9aa3\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"30\" font-family=\"Georgia\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#3a2a10\">↶</text></svg>","body":"<p>Each operation has an <b>inverse</b> that undoes it: − undoes +, and ÷ undoes ×.</p><p>To run a machine backwards, undo the steps in <b>reverse order</b>.</p><p>IN → × 3 → + 2 → OUT. &nbsp; Backwards: OUT → − 2 → ÷ 3 → IN.</p>","room":"The Machine Hall","lesson":"Lesson 5 · Changing the subject"},{"title":"Tape measure","icon":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\"><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"50\" r=\"30\" fill=\"#e0c03a\" stroke=\"#8a6d1a\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"50\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#8a6d1a\"/><rect x=\"60\" y=\"68\" width=\"34\" height=\"12\" fill=\"#f0d870\" stroke=\"#8a6d1a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g stroke=\"#3a2a10\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><path d=\"M66 68v5M72 68v5M78 68v5M84 68v5M90 68v5\"/></g></svg>","body":"<p>1 cm = 10 mm &nbsp; · &nbsp; 1 m = 100 cm &nbsp; · &nbsp; 1 km = 1000 m &nbsp; · &nbsp; 1 kg = 1000 g</p><p>To a <b>smaller</b> unit, <b>multiply</b>: 2.5 m = 2.5 × 100 = 250 cm.</p><p>To a <b>larger</b> unit, <b>divide</b>: 350 cm = 350 ÷ 100 = 3.5 m.</p>","room":"The Measuring Room","lesson":"Lesson 6 · Using and checking formulae in context"}]};
